Post Date: 2020-07-07T16:38:33Z
Current Date: April 4 2025
Title: Compiler warning CS8618: How can I get around it.
Description: **Net Standard 2.1**: 

**Steps to Reproduce**:
See following code:
```
public class Class1
{
  public string MyProperty { get; set; }
  public string MyProperty2 { get; set; }
  public string MyProperty3 { get; set; }

  public Class1() //Warning CS8618
  {
    Init();
  }

  public Class1(string myproperty2) //Warning CS8618
  {
    Init();
    MyProperty2 = myproperty2;
  }

  private void Init()
  {
    MyProperty = "";
    MyProperty2 = "";
    MyProperty3 = "";
  }
}
```

Is there a way to tell the compiler that the Init() function takes care of initializing the properties?


